{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QqqvHdHjhFUJCCEquX8C1c","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Brief: ntfy notifications for instance admins\n2\t\n3\ttype: feature\n4\tid: around\n5\tbranch: feature/around_ntfy-notifications-for-instance-admins\n6\tdate: 2026-10-14\n7\tauthor: Leander Muskalla\n8\t\n9\t## What\n10\t\n11\tWire up the ntfy admin notifications added in solyto/api (`337a3e1`) for\n12\tself-hosters:\n13\t\n14\t- `compose.yml`: top-level secrets `ntfy_topic` and `ntfy_token`. On `api` and\n15\t  `queue`, add `NTFY_TOPIC_FILE=/run/secrets/ntfy_topic`,\n16\t  `NTFY_TOKEN_FILE=/run/secrets/ntfy_token` and the service-level `secrets:`\n17\t  entries.\n18\t- `setup.sh`: add `write_empty \"ntfy_topic\"` and `write_empty \"ntfy_token\"` to\n19\t  the optional secrets.\n20\t- `.env`: `NTFY_URL=` (empty) in its own block.\n21\t- `README.md`: list `ntfy_topic` and `ntfy_token` under optional secrets and\n22\t  note that ntfy is off unless URL and topic are both set.\n23\t\n24\t## Why\n25\t\n26\tThe API now reads `NTFY_URL` from env and `NTFY_TOPIC` / `NTFY_TOKEN` via\n27\t`DockerSecretHelper`. Without these changes self-hosters can't enable it.\n28\t\n29\t## Decisions\n30\t\n31\t- Secrets go on `api` and `queue` only (`api` evaluates `via()`, `queue`\n32\t  sends). `dav`, `nginx` and `imgproxy` need nothing.\n33\t- No defaults and no fallback to ntfy.sh: an instance makes no outbound call\n34\t  unless the operator sets URL and topic.\n35\t\n36\t## Out of scope\n37\t\n38\t- Any change to the API itself.\n39\t\n40\t## Notes\n41\t\n42\t- The `write_empty` entries are required: compose fails on a missing secret\n43\t  file. An empty file is fine, the API checks with `filled()`.\n44\t- Existing installs need to create the two secret files manually (or rerun the\n45\t  relevant part of `setup.sh`) before pulling the new `compose.yml`.\n46\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8c1730cf-4086-4c64-9fed-80b109264b43","uuid":"b92effce-164d-4ad7-9352-c5bc7f61990c","timestamp":"2026-10-14T20:33:41.613Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/around_ntfy-notifications-for-instance-admins/brief.md","content":"# Brief: ntfy notifications for instance admins\n\ntype: feature\nid: around\nbranch: feature/around_ntfy-notifications-for-instance-admins\ndate: 2026-10-14\nauthor: Leander Muskalla\n\n## What\n\nWire up the ntfy admin notifications added in solyto/api (`337a3e1`) for\nself-hosters:\n\n- `compose.yml`: top-level secrets `ntfy_topic` and `ntfy_token`. On `api` and\n  `queue`, add `NTFY_TOPIC_FILE=/run/secrets/ntfy_topic`,\n  `NTFY_TOKEN_FILE=/run/secrets/ntfy_token` and the service-level `secrets:`\n  entries.\n- `setup.sh`: add `write_empty \"ntfy_topic\"` and `write_empty \"ntfy_token\"` to\n  the optional secrets.\n- `.env`: `NTFY_URL=` (empty) in its own block.\n- `README.md`: list `ntfy_topic` and `ntfy_token` under optional secrets and\n  note that ntfy is off unless URL and topic are both set.\n\n## Why\n\nThe API now reads `NTFY_URL` from env and `NTFY_TOPIC` / `NTFY_TOKEN` via\n`DockerSecretHelper`. Without these changes self-hosters can't enable it.\n\n## Decisions\n\n- Secrets go on `api` and `queue` only (`api` evaluates `via()`, `queue`\n  sends). `dav`, `nginx` and `imgproxy` need nothing.\n- No defaults and no fallback to ntfy.sh: an instance makes no outbound call\n  unless the operator sets URL and topic.\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- Any change to the API itself.\n\n## Notes\n\n- The `write_empty` entries are required: compose fails on a missing secret\n  file. An empty file is fine, the API checks with `filled()`.\n- Existing installs need to create the two secret files manually (or rerun the\n  relevant part of `setup.sh`) before pulling the new `compose.yml`.\n","numLines":46,"startLine":1,"totalLines":46}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01QqqvHdHjhFUJCCEquX8C1c","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
