{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01G3DtcLDkBrp1AszqVTRgKN","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Implementation: Fix setup.sh for all OSes\n2\t\n3\tid: plus\n4\tdeveloper: @developer\n5\tdate: 2026-10-14\n6\t\n7\t## Summary\n8\t\n9\t`setup.sh` no longer looks up the user name `www-data` on the host. It now\n10\t`chown`s `storage/` to a numeric UID/GID (default 33:33, which is www-data\n11\tinside the `solyto/api-php` containers). You can override it with `SOLYTO_UID` /\n12\t`SOLYTO_GID`. The README explains the ownership step and how to fix it by hand.\n13\tTASK-2 was **not** implemented because tasks.md marks it as needing human\n14\tconfirmation, and this session ran unattended.\n15\t\n16\t## Changes\n17\t\n18\tTASK-1: `setup.sh` — added `SOLYTO_UID`/`SOLYTO_GID` (default 33, can be overridden from the\n19\tenv) near the top, with a comment on why the IDs are numeric. Replaced\n20\t`chown -R www-data:www-data storage/` with `chown -R \"${SOLYTO_UID}:${SOLYTO_GID}\" storage/`.\n21\tChecked with `bash -n`.\n22\t\n23\tTASK-2: skipped (needs human confirmation). It is about warning or using sudo\n24\tinstead of stopping when not running as root.\n25\t\n26\tTASK-3: `README.md` — added a note under \"Install script\": storage/ is owned by 33:33\n27\t(container www-data), you need root/`sudo bash`, how to use `SOLYTO_UID`/`SOLYTO_GID`,\n28\tand the manual `sudo chown -R 33:33 solyto/storage` fix. The wording matches the\n29\tcurrent behaviour (the script stops if chown fails). Update it if TASK-2 is approved.\n30\t\n31\t## Known issues / follow-ups\n32\t\n33\t- Not yet confirmed that `www-data` in `solyto/api-php` is UID/GID 33. Docker was not\n34\t  available in this session. Please run\n35\t  `docker run --rm --entrypoint id solyto/api-php:latest www-data` before merging.\n36\t  (The Arch fix with 33:33 suggests it is.)\n37\t- TASK-2 is waiting for a decision.\n38\t- `sed -i -e …` in setup.sh only works with GNU sed and will break on macOS/BSD.\n39\t  This is open question 1 in tasks.md and was not in scope.\n40\t- The working tree shows `/workspace/.env` as modified, but git cannot hash it\n41\t  (\"unsupported file type\", probably a mount). It was not touched or committed.\n42\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8c1730cf-4086-4c64-9fed-80b109264b43","uuid":"6674c64d-53a4-425c-9b10-579ab12dee1f","timestamp":"2026-10-14T20:34:01.676Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/archive/plus_fix-setup-sh-for-all-oses/implementation.md","content":"# Implementation: Fix setup.sh for all OSes\n\nid: plus\ndeveloper: @developer\ndate: 2026-10-14\n\n## Summary\n\n`setup.sh` no longer looks up the user name `www-data` on the host. It now\n`chown`s `storage/` to a numeric UID/GID (default 33:33, which is www-data\ninside the `solyto/api-php` containers). You can override it with `SOLYTO_UID` /\n`SOLYTO_GID`. The README explains the ownership step and how to fix it by hand.\nTASK-2 was **not** implemented because tasks.md marks it as needing human\nconfirmation, and this session ran unattended.\n\n## Changes\n\nTASK-1: `setup.sh` — added `SOLYTO_UID`/`SOLYTO_GID` (default 33, can be overridden from the\nenv) near the top, with a comment on why the IDs are numeric. Replaced\n`chown -R www-data:www-data storage/` with `chown -R \"${SOLYTO_UID}:${SOLYTO_GID}\" storage/`.\nChecked with `bash -n`.\n\nTASK-2: skipped (needs human confirmation). It is about warning or using sudo\ninstead of stopping when not running as root.\n\nTASK-3: `README.md` — added a note under \"Install script\": storage/ is owned by 33:33\n(container www-data), you need root/`sudo bash`, how to use `SOLYTO_UID`/`SOLYTO_GID`,\nand the manual `sudo chown -R 33:33 solyto/storage` fix. The wording matches the\ncurrent behaviour (the script stops if chown fails). Update it if TASK-2 is approved.\n\n## Known issues / follow-ups\n\n- Not yet confirmed that `www-data` in `solyto/api-php` is UID/GID 33. Docker was not\n  available in this session. Please run\n  `docker run --rm --entrypoint id solyto/api-php:latest www-data` before merging.\n  (The Arch fix with 33:33 suggests it is.)\n- TASK-2 is waiting for a decision.\n- `sed -i -e …` in setup.sh only works with GNU sed and will break on macOS/BSD.\n  This is open question 1 in tasks.md and was not in scope.\n- The working tree shows `/workspace/.env` as modified, but git cannot hash it\n  (\"unsupported file type\", probably a mount). It was not touched or committed.\n","numLines":42,"startLine":1,"totalLines":42}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01G3DtcLDkBrp1AszqVTRgKN","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
