{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","content":"Exit code 1\nbrief.md\nimplementation.md\nsession.log\ntasks.md\ntokens.json\nverdict.md\n# Brief: ntfy notifications for instance admins\n\ntype: feature\nid: around\nbranch: feature/around_ntfy-notifications-for-instance-admins\ndate: 2026-10-14\nauthor: Leander Muskalla\n\n## What\n\nWire up the ntfy admin notifications added in solyto/api (`337a3e1`) for\nself-hosters:\n\n- `compose.yml`: top-level secrets `ntfy_topic` and `ntfy_token`. On `api` and\n  `queue`, add `NTFY_TOPIC_FILE=/run/secrets/ntfy_topic`,\n  `NTFY_TOKEN_FILE=/run/secrets/ntfy_token` and the service-level `secrets:`\n  entries.\n- `setup.sh`: add `write_empty \"ntfy_topic\"` and `write_empty \"ntfy_token\"` to\n  the optional secrets.\n- `.env`: `NTFY_URL=` (empty) in its own block.\n- `README.md`: list `ntfy_topic` and `ntfy_token` under optional secrets and\n  note that ntfy is off unless URL and topic are both set.\n\n## Why\n\nThe API now reads `NTFY_URL` from env and `NTFY_TOPIC` / `NTFY_TOKEN` via\n`DockerSecretHelper`. Without these changes self-hosters can't enable it.\n\n## Decisions\n\n- Secrets go on `api` and `queue` only (`api` evaluates `via()`, `queue`\n  sends). `dav`, `nginx` and `imgproxy` need nothing.\n- No defaults and no fallback to ntfy.sh: an instance makes no outbound call\n  unless the operator sets URL and topic.\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- Any change to the API itself.\n\n## Notes\n\n- The `write_empty` entries are required: compose fails on a missing secret\n  file. An empty file is fine, the API checks with `filled()`.\n- Existing installs need to create the two secret files manually (or rerun the\n  relevant part of `setup.sh`) before pulling the new `compose.yml`.\nfeature/around_ntfy-notifications-for-instance-admins\n# Tasks: ntfy notifications for instance admins\n\nid: around\nanalyst: @analyst\ndate: 2026-10-14\n\n<!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n\n## Findings from reading the repo (input for the developer)\n\n- Branch checked: the worktree HEAD is `feature/around_ntfy-notifications-for-instance-admins`,\n  which matches the brief.\n- `compose.yml`:\n  - `api` sets `*_FILE` env vars in its `environment:` map (l.78-94) and lists its\n    service secrets at l.98-114. The last entries are `IMGPROXY_SALT_FILE` / `imgproxy_salt`.\n  - `queue` follows the same pattern: env vars at l.169-182, secrets at l.186-199.\n  - The top-level `secrets:` block is at l.317-353. Every entry has the form\n    `name:\\n    file: ./secrets/name`.\n  - `api` and `queue` both use `env_file: \".env\"`, so a new `NTFY_URL` in `.env` gets\n    to both containers without any `environment:` entry. **Don't** add `NTFY_URL` to\n    compose (the brief doesn't ask for it).\n- `setup.sh`: the optional secrets are the `write_empty` calls at l.83-93, and the last\n  one is `bgg_api_key`.\n- `README.md`: the secrets file tree is at l.89-111, with inline `# optional` comments on\n  some entries. The \"Required vs optional secrets\" bullet list is at l.141-157.\n- **`.env` can't be edited in this sandbox.** `/workspace/.env` reads as 0 bytes.\n  Earlier jobs (`docs/jobs/archive/show_…/implementation.md`,\n  `docs/jobs/archive/plus_…/implementation.md`) found that it is a `/dev/null` character\n  device mounted over the real file, and git reports it as \"modified / unsupported file\n  type\". Upstream `.env` has blocks separated by blank lines, e.g. AI (~l.69-73),\n  Mail (~l.75-78), Image driver (~l.80-81), Telegram debug (~l.84-85). See TASK-3 for how\n  to handle this.\n\n## Task breakdown\n\nTASK-1: In `compose.yml`, add top-level secrets `ntfy_topic` and `ntfy_token` (`file: ./secrets/ntfy_topic` / `./secrets/ntfy_token`). Add `NTFY_TOPIC_FILE: /run/secrets/ntfy_topic` and `NTFY_TOKEN_FILE: /run/secrets/ntfy_token` to the `environment:` of **`api` and `queue` only**, plus `ntfy_topic` / `ntfy_token` to those two services' `secrets:` lists.\n     files: compose.yml\n     depends: none\n     risk: medium — a typo or a service-level secret with no top-level definition stops the whole stack from starting, and existing installs without the two secret files will fail on `docker compose up` (expected per the brief, see TASK-2/4). Verify: if Docker is available, run `docker compose config` with stub `secrets/ntfy_*` files; otherwise at least parse the YAML. Confirm that `dav`, `nginx` and `imgproxy` are unchanged.\n     note: do all three parts in one change. Splitting them would leave compose.yml invalid in between.\n\nTASK-2: In `setup.sh`, add `write_empty \"ntfy_topic\"` and `write_empty \"ntfy_token\"` to the optional-secrets block (after `write_empty \"bgg_api_key\"`, l.93).\n     files: setup.sh\n     depends: none (logically pairs with TASK-1: without it, fresh installs fail on the new compose secrets)\n     risk: low — two extra lines that use an existing idempotent helper. Verify with `bash -n setup.sh`.\n\nTASK-3: In `.env`, add `NTFY_URL=` (empty, no default) in its own block, i.e. separated by blank lines, ideally with a short comment header matching the style of the neighbouring blocks.\n     files: .env\n     depends: none\n     risk: high (process, not code) — in this sandbox `.env` is a `/dev/null` mount, so edits are silently discarded and the real file can't be committed from here. The developer should first check this (`test -c .env` / `git status`). If it is still masked, **don't** try workarounds such as writing blobs to the git index by hand. Skip the task and record in implementation.md the exact block a human should add outside the sandbox. Don't commit `.env` either way unless it is a real, readable file with the full upstream content plus the new block.\n\nTASK-4: In `README.md`, add `ntfy_topic` and `ntfy_token` to the secrets file tree (l.89-111, marked `# optional`) and add a bullet to the optional-secrets list (l.141-157). The bullet should cover what they are for (admin notifications via ntfy), that `NTFY_URL` is set in `.env`, and that ntfy is **off unless both `NTFY_URL` and `ntfy_topic` are set**, with no default server and no outbound calls otherwise. `ntfy_token` is optional (for protected topics).\n     files: README.md\n     depends: TASK-1, TASK-3 (names must match what was actually added)\n     risk: low — docs only. The one risk is describing app behaviour this repo can't verify (see open questions), so stick to what the brief states.\n\n## Open questions / unclear scope (not tasks, don't do these without a decision)\n\n1. **Upgrade note for existing installs.** The brief notes that existing installs must\n   create `secrets/ntfy_topic` and `secrets/ntfy_token` before pulling the new\n   `compose.yml`, or the stack won't start. The README \"Updates\" section (l.298-300)\n   currently says \"just pull the newest image and restart\". The brief doesn't ask for a\n   README change here, so it isn't a task. A human should decide whether to add a\n   one-line upgrade note, since this is a breaking change for current self-hosters.\n2. **Format of `NTFY_URL`.** It isn't clear from this repo whether `NTFY_URL` is the\n   server base URL (e.g. `https://ntfy.example.com`) or includes the topic, or which\n   events trigger notifications. That lives in solyto/api `337a3e1`. The README should not\n   claim specifics beyond \"ntfy server URL\" unless the developer can confirm them from\n   that commit.\n3. The `.env` mount issue (TASK-3) needs a human to apply that one-line change outside\n   the sandbox.\n# Implementation: ntfy notifications for instance admins\n\nid: around\ndeveloper: @developer\ndate: 2026-10-14\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded the plumbing self-hosters need for the ntfy admin notifications from solyto/api `337a3e1`. That covers the compose secrets and env vars on `api` and `queue`, empty secret files from `setup.sh`, and README docs. The `.env` change (TASK-3) could not be made in this sandbox and has to be applied by hand (see below).\n\n## Changes\n\nTASK-1: `compose.yml`: added top-level secrets `ntfy_topic` / `ntfy_token` (`file: ./secrets/ntfy_*`). Added `NTFY_TOPIC_FILE` / `NTFY_TOKEN_FILE` (`/run/secrets/ntfy_*`) to the `environment:` of `api` and `queue`, plus matching service-level `secrets:` entries. `dav`, `nginx`, `imgproxy` and the others are unchanged. Verification: no Docker and no YAML parser were available in the sandbox, so `docker compose config` was not run. I checked the diff by hand: the indentation matches the neighbouring entries, and both service-level secrets have top-level definitions.\n\nTASK-2: `setup.sh`: added `write_empty \"ntfy_topic\"` and `write_empty \"ntfy_token\"` after `bgg_api_key` in the optional-secrets block. `bash -n setup.sh` passes.\n\nTASK-3: **Not done (skipped as the plan says).** `/workspace/.env` is still a `/dev/null` character device in this sandbox (`crw-rw-rw- 1,3`), so edits are discarded and it can't be committed. A human should add this block to `.env` outside the sandbox, after the `# Image processing` block (the committed `.env` has `IMAGE_DRIVER=intervention` followed by two blank lines, then `# Telegram bot`):\n\n```\n# ntfy (admin notifications)\n# Base URL of your ntfy server. Leave empty to disable ntfy.\nNTFY_URL=\n```\n\nTASK-4: `README.md`: added `ntfy_topic` / `ntfy_token` (marked optional) to the secrets file tree. Also added a bullet to the optional-secrets list covering what they are for, `NTFY_URL` in `.env`, `ntfy_token` only being needed for protected topics, and that ntfy is off unless both `NTFY_URL` and `ntfy_topic` are set, with no default server and no outbound calls otherwise.\n\n## Known issues / follow-ups\n\n- TASK-3 `.env` block above needs to be applied manually.\n- **Breaking for existing installs:** `docker compose up` will fail until `secrets/ntfy_topic` and `secrets/ntfy_token` exist (e.g. `touch secrets/ntfy_topic secrets/ntfy_token`). The README \"Updates\" section doesn't mention this. A human should decide whether to add an upgrade note (open question 1 in tasks.md).\n- I couldn't confirm the exact `NTFY_URL` format (base URL vs. including the topic) from this repo. The README and the suggested `.env` comment assume a server base URL, which fits the topic coming from a separate secret. Worth checking against solyto/api `337a3e1`.\n- `compose.yml` not checked with `docker compose config` (no Docker in the sandbox).\ncat: /workspace/.manigot/manigot.json: No such file or directory","is_error":true,"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LQGN6KQQyz8Qg1FmioSt9k"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9eacb543-dd37-42d8-83e8-35267f1e12c8","uuid":"dc2464cb-71e9-4692-ae81-acfd6fa19271","timestamp":"2026-10-14T20:35:42.803Z","tool_use_result":"Error: Exit code 1\nbrief.md\nimplementation.md\nsession.log\ntasks.md\ntokens.json\nverdict.md\n# Brief: ntfy notifications for instance admins\n\ntype: feature\nid: around\nbranch: feature/around_ntfy-notifications-for-instance-admins\ndate: 2026-10-14\nauthor: Leander Muskalla\n\n## What\n\nWire up the ntfy admin notifications added in solyto/api (`337a3e1`) for\nself-hosters:\n\n- `compose.yml`: top-level secrets `ntfy_topic` and `ntfy_token`. On `api` and\n  `queue`, add `NTFY_TOPIC_FILE=/run/secrets/ntfy_topic`,\n  `NTFY_TOKEN_FILE=/run/secrets/ntfy_token` and the service-level `secrets:`\n  entries.\n- `setup.sh`: add `write_empty \"ntfy_topic\"` and `write_empty \"ntfy_token\"` to\n  the optional secrets.\n- `.env`: `NTFY_URL=` (empty) in its own block.\n- `README.md`: list `ntfy_topic` and `ntfy_token` under optional secrets and\n  note that ntfy is off unless URL and topic are both set.\n\n## Why\n\nThe API now reads `NTFY_URL` from env and `NTFY_TOPIC` / `NTFY_TOKEN` via\n`DockerSecretHelper`. Without these changes self-hosters can't enable it.\n\n## Decisions\n\n- Secrets go on `api` and `queue` only (`api` evaluates `via()`, `queue`\n  sends). `dav`, `nginx` and `imgproxy` need nothing.\n- No defaults and no fallback to ntfy.sh: an instance makes no ou